IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cla-core`
IMPORT `cla-child-abuse`

-- Civil Liability Act 2002 (NSW) -- worked cases for every exported question in cla-child-abuse.l4 (Parts 1B and 1C).
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from the encoding's output. Each
-- assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. The commencement dates used here
-- (section 6F, section 6H and Part 1B: 1 December 2018; Limitation Act s 6A: 17 March 2016) are ILLUSTRATIVE: the
-- deposited text does not give them. Check the NSW legislation website.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases -- Parts 1B and 1C`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`

`commenced` MEANS `d` 1 12 2018
`s 6A commenced` MEANS `d` 17 3 2016

`sexual` MEANS `sexual abuse`
`physical` MEANS `physical abuse`
`other abuse` MEANS `another kind of abuse, such as emotional or psychological abuse or neglect`

`exercised` MEANS `it exercised care, supervision or authority over me, or claimed to, or was obliged by law to`
`delegated` MEANS `it delegated care, supervision or authority over me, wholly or partly, to another organisation`
`no standing` MEANS `none of these`

`officer` MEANS `an office holder, officer, employee, owner, volunteer or contractor of the organisation`
`religious` MEANS `a religious leader or member of the personnel of the organisation, which is a religious organisation`
`carer` MEANS `an authorised carer authorised by the organisation as a designated agency under the Children's Guardian Act 2019`
`delegate's person` MEANS `someone associated with another organisation to which this organisation delegated care, supervision or authority over me`
`funder only` MEANS `someone linked to it only because the organisation funds or regulates another organisation`
`stranger` MEANS `someone else`

`so` MEANS `the court has found that it is so`
`not so` MEANS `the court has found that it is not so`
`undecided` MEANS `the court has not decided`

`presumed` MEANS `the organisation is presumed to have breached its duty to me, unless it proves it took reasonable precautions`
`breached` MEANS `the organisation breached its duty: the presumption stands because it did not prove reasonable precautions`
`rebutted` MEANS `the presumption is rebutted: the court found the organisation took reasonable precautions`
`too early` MEANS `section 6F does not apply: the abuse happened before section 6F commenced`
`no 6F claim` MEANS `section 6F gives me no claim on these facts`
`6F open` MEANS `the Act does not settle it`

`employee` MEANS `as its employee`
`akin` MEANS `not as its employee, but carrying out activities as an integral part of its activities and for its benefit`
`neither` MEANS `in neither of those ways`

`may apply` MEANS `I may apply for the court to appoint the trustees of an associated trust as proper defendant`
`not yet` MEANS `not yet: the 120 days after service have not ended`
`appointed in time` MEANS `no: a suitable proper defendant was appointed in time and is still suitable`
`State is defendant` MEANS `no: the State is taken to be the proper defendant for a public sector body`
`incorporated` MEANS `no: section 6N is for unincorporated organisations`

`general` MEANS `negligence, or another claim for death or personal injury not listed here`
`against the abuser` MEANS `sexual assault or other sexual misconduct by the defendant`
`vicarious` MEANS `vicarious liability for someone else's intentional act or sexual misconduct`
`work injury` MEANS `work injury damages against an employer under Division 3 of Part 5 of the Workers Compensation Act 1987`

`in time` MEANS `the organisation identified its associated trusts within the 28 days`
`still running` MEANS `the 28 days have not ended and the organisation has not yet identified its associated trusts`
`missed` MEANS `the organisation did not identify its associated trusts within the 28 days`

§§ `s 6F -- the duty and the reverse onus`

-- Arguments: day of abuse, day s 6F commenced, age, kind, lawful, the State itself, how the organisation stood to me,
-- who the abuser was, connected with its responsibility, the court's finding on reasonable precautions.
-- The plain case: a 12-year-old abused by an officer of an organisation caring for the child, nothing decided yet.
#ASSERT `What does section 6F mean for my claim` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commenced` 12 `sexual` FALSE FALSE `exercised` `officer` TRUE `undecided` EQUALS `presumed`
-- The court's finding on reasonable precautions (s 6F(3)).
#ASSERT `What does section 6F mean for my claim` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commenced` 12 `sexual` FALSE FALSE `exercised` `officer` TRUE `so` EQUALS `rebutted`
#ASSERT `What does section 6F mean for my claim` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commenced` 12 `sexual` FALSE FALSE `exercised` `officer` TRUE `not so` EQUALS `breached`
-- Sch 1 cl 43: abuse on the commencement day counts (fork F2); the day before does not.
#ASSERT `What does section 6F mean for my claim` (`d` 1 12 2018) `commenced` 12 `sexual` FALSE FALSE `exercised` `officer` TRUE `undecided` EQUALS `presumed`
#ASSERT `What does section 6F mean for my claim` (`d` 30 11 2018) `commenced` 12 `sexual` FALSE FALSE `exercised` `officer` TRUE `undecided` EQUALS `too early`
-- s 6A child: under 18.
#ASSERT `What does section 6F mean for my claim` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commenced` 17 `sexual` FALSE FALSE `exercised` `officer` TRUE `undecided` EQUALS `presumed`
#ASSERT `What does section 6F mean for my claim` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commenced` 18 `sexual` FALSE FALSE `exercised` `officer` TRUE `undecided` EQUALS `no 6F claim`
-- s 6F(5): sexual or physical abuse, not lawful at the time.
#ASSERT `What does section 6F mean for my claim` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commenced` 12 `physical` FALSE FALSE `exercised` `officer` TRUE `undecided` EQUALS `presumed`
#ASSERT `What does section 6F mean for my claim` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commenced` 12 `other abuse` FALSE FALSE `exercised` `officer` TRUE `undecided` EQUALS `no 6F claim`
#ASSERT `What does section 6F mean for my claim` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commenced` 12 `physical` TRUE FALSE `exercised` `officer` TRUE `undecided` EQUALS `no 6F claim`
-- s 6A: an organisation does not include the State.
#ASSERT `What does section 6F mean for my claim` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commenced` 12 `sexual` FALSE TRUE `exercised` `officer` TRUE `undecided` EQUALS `no 6F claim`
-- s 6D: responsibility, including by delegation.
#ASSERT `What does section 6F mean for my claim` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commenced` 12 `sexual` FALSE FALSE `delegated` `officer` TRUE `undecided` EQUALS `presumed`
#ASSERT `What does section 6F mean for my claim` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commenced` 12 `sexual` FALSE FALSE `no standing` `officer` TRUE `undecided` EQUALS `no 6F claim`
-- s 6E: the listed associates; funding or regulating only (s 6E(2)); anyone else is open.
#ASSERT `What does section 6F mean for my claim` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commenced` 12 `sexual` FALSE FALSE `exercised` `religious` TRUE `undecided` EQUALS `presumed`
#ASSERT `What does section 6F mean for my claim` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commenced` 12 `sexual` FALSE FALSE `exercised` `carer` TRUE `undecided` EQUALS `presumed`
#ASSERT `What does section 6F mean for my claim` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commenced` 12 `sexual` FALSE FALSE `delegated` `delegate's person` TRUE `undecided` EQUALS `presumed`
#ASSERT `What does section 6F mean for my claim` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commenced` 12 `sexual` FALSE FALSE `exercised` `funder only` TRUE `undecided` EQUALS `no 6F claim`
#ASSERT `What does section 6F mean for my claim` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commenced` 12 `sexual` FALSE FALSE `exercised` `stranger` TRUE `undecided` EQUALS `6F open`
#ASSERT `What does section 6F mean for my claim` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commenced` 12 `sexual` FALSE FALSE `exercised` `stranger` TRUE `so` EQUALS `6F open`
-- A failed condition beats the open one.
#ASSERT `What does section 6F mean for my claim` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commenced` 12 `sexual` FALSE FALSE `exercised` `stranger` FALSE `undecided` EQUALS `no 6F claim`
-- Not in connection with the organisation's responsibility.
#ASSERT `What does section 6F mean for my claim` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commenced` 12 `sexual` FALSE FALSE `exercised` `officer` FALSE `undecided` EQUALS `no 6F claim`

§§ `ss 6G, 6H -- vicarious liability`

-- Arguments: day, day s 6H commenced, age, kind, lawful, State itself, how the abuser worked, independent business,
-- authorised carer, the court's finding on the occasion, took advantage.
#ASSERT `Is the organisation vicariously liable under section 6H` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commenced` 12 `sexual` FALSE FALSE `employee` FALSE FALSE `so` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the organisation vicariously liable under section 6H` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commenced` 12 `sexual` FALSE FALSE `employee` FALSE FALSE `not so` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the organisation vicariously liable under section 6H` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commenced` 12 `sexual` FALSE FALSE `employee` FALSE FALSE `undecided` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 6H(1)(b): took advantage of the occasion; a failed condition beats the undecided finding.
#ASSERT `Is the organisation vicariously liable under section 6H` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commenced` 12 `sexual` FALSE FALSE `employee` FALSE FALSE `so` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the organisation vicariously liable under section 6H` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commenced` 12 `sexual` FALSE FALSE `employee` FALSE FALSE `undecided` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 6G: akin to an employee, and its two exclusions; the exclusions do not touch a real employee.
#ASSERT `Is the organisation vicariously liable under section 6H` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commenced` 12 `sexual` FALSE FALSE `akin` FALSE FALSE `so` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the organisation vicariously liable under section 6H` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commenced` 12 `sexual` FALSE FALSE `akin` TRUE FALSE `so` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the organisation vicariously liable under section 6H` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commenced` 12 `sexual` FALSE FALSE `akin` FALSE TRUE `so` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the organisation vicariously liable under section 6H` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commenced` 12 `sexual` FALSE FALSE `employee` TRUE FALSE `so` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the organisation vicariously liable under section 6H` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commenced` 12 `sexual` FALSE FALSE `neither` FALSE FALSE `so` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Sch 1 cl 44: the commencement day and the day before.
#ASSERT `Is the organisation vicariously liable under section 6H` (`d` 1 12 2018) `commenced` 12 `sexual` FALSE FALSE `employee` FALSE FALSE `so` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the organisation vicariously liable under section 6H` (`d` 30 11 2018) `commenced` 12 `sexual` FALSE FALSE `employee` FALSE FALSE `so` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Child, kind of abuse, lawful act, the State.
#ASSERT `Is the organisation vicariously liable under section 6H` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commenced` 18 `sexual` FALSE FALSE `employee` FALSE FALSE `so` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the organisation vicariously liable under section 6H` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commenced` 12 `physical` FALSE FALSE `employee` FALSE FALSE `so` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the organisation vicariously liable under section 6H` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commenced` 12 `other abuse` FALSE FALSE `employee` FALSE FALSE `so` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the organisation vicariously liable under section 6H` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commenced` 12 `physical` TRUE FALSE `employee` FALSE FALSE `so` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the organisation vicariously liable under section 6H` (`d` 1 6 2020) `commenced` 12 `sexual` FALSE TRUE `employee` FALSE FALSE `so` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 6C -- successor organisations`

#ASSERT `Is the successor the same organisation under Part 1B` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the successor the same organisation under Part 1B` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

