-- s 6N(1): 120 days after service. Served 1 March 2024: day 120 is 29 June 2024 (30 + 30 + 31 + 29 days).
#ASSERT `By when must a proper defendant be appointed` (`d` 1 3 2024) EQUALS `d` 29 6 2024
-- Served 15 January 2023: 16 + 28 + 31 + 30 + 15 = 120, so 15 May 2023.
#ASSERT `By when must a proper defendant be appointed` (`d` 15 1 2023) EQUALS `d` 15 5 2023

-- ss 6L, 6N. Arguments: incorporated, public sector body, day served, appointed, day appointed, ceased to be suitable,
-- day I would apply. Served 1 March 2024; the 120 days end with 29 June 2024 (fork F4).
#ASSERT `Can I apply for the trustees to be appointed` FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 3 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 30 6 2024) EQUALS `may apply`
#ASSERT `Can I apply for the trustees to be appointed` FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 3 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 29 6 2024) EQUALS `not yet`
#ASSERT `Can I apply for the trustees to be appointed` FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 3 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 4 2024) EQUALS `not yet`
-- Appointed on day 120 is in time; appointed on day 121 is not, so the section applies (finding 6).
#ASSERT `Can I apply for the trustees to be appointed` FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 3 2024) TRUE (`d` 29 6 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 8 2024) EQUALS `appointed in time`
#ASSERT `Can I apply for the trustees to be appointed` FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 3 2024) TRUE (`d` 30 6 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 8 2024) EQUALS `may apply`
-- s 6N(1)(b): appointed in time, but ceased to be suitable afterwards.
#ASSERT `Can I apply for the trustees to be appointed` FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 3 2024) TRUE (`d` 1 4 2024) TRUE (`d` 1 8 2024) EQUALS `may apply`
#ASSERT `Can I apply for the trustees to be appointed` FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 3 2024) TRUE (`d` 1 4 2024) TRUE (`d` 15 6 2024) EQUALS `not yet`
-- s 6L(3) public sector body; an incorporated organisation.
#ASSERT `Can I apply for the trustees to be appointed` FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 8 2024) EQUALS `State is defendant`
#ASSERT `Can I apply for the trustees to be appointed` TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 3 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 8 2024) EQUALS `incorporated`

-- s 6N(4): 28 days after the application. 10 January 2025 + 28 = 7 February 2025; 1 February 2024 + 28 = 29 February
-- 2024 (a leap year).
#ASSERT `By when must the organisation identify its trusts` (`d` 10 1 2025) EQUALS `d` 7 2 2025
#ASSERT `By when must the organisation identify its trusts` (`d` 1 2 2024) EQUALS `d` 29 2 2024

-- s 6N(4) as a regulative rule. Arguments: day I applied, identified, day identified, today. Applied 1 February 2024.
#ASSERT `Has the organisation identified its trusts in time` (`d` 1 2 2024) TRUE (`d` 29 2 2024) (`d` 1 3 2024) EQUALS `in time`
#ASSERT `Has the organisation identified its trusts in time` (`d` 1 2 2024) TRUE (`d` 1 3 2024) (`d` 1 3 2024) EQUALS `missed`
#ASSERT `Has the organisation identified its trusts in time` (`d` 1 2 2024) TRUE (`d` 10 2 2024) (`d` 10 2 2024) EQUALS `in time`
#ASSERT `Has the organisation identified its trusts in time` (`d` 1 2 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 29 2 2024) EQUALS `still running`
#ASSERT `Has the organisation identified its trusts in time` (`d` 1 2 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 1 2 2024) EQUALS `still running`
#ASSERT `Has the organisation identified its trusts in time` (`d` 1 2 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 1 3 2024) EQUALS `missed`

-- s 6O. Arguments: incorporated, a proper defendant appointed.
